{'input': {'source_code': '@SuppressWarnings("unchecked")\npublic static Map<String, String> deserializeOffsetMap(String lastSourceOffset) throws IOException {\n  Map<String, String> offsetMap;\n  if (lastSourceOffset == null || lastSourceOffset.isEmpty()) {    \n    offsetMap = new HashMap<>();  \n  } else {\n    offsetMap = JSON_MAPPER.readValue(lastSourceOffset, Map.class);  \n  }\n  return offsetMap;\n}\n', 'repo_info': {'repo': 'streamsets/datacollector', 'path': 'stagesupport/src/main/java/com/.../OffsetUtil.java', 'function_name': 'OffsetUtil.deserializeOffsetMap'}}, 'output': 'The provided code is a static method named `deserializeOffsetMap` in the Java class located at `stagesupport/src/main/java/com/.../OffsetUtil.java`. This method takes a single parameter: `lastSourceOffset`, which is of type `String`.\n\nHere\'s an explanation of what this method does:\n\n1. The method uses the `@SuppressWarnings("unchecked")` annotation to suppress unchecked warnings, indicating that it handles potential unchecked or unsafe operations.\n\n2. It declares a variable named `offsetMap` of type `Map<String, String>`, which will store the deserialized offset data.\n\n3. The method checks if the `lastSourceOffset` parameter is either null or an empty string using the condition `if (lastSourceOffset == null || lastSourceOffset.isEmpty())`.\n\n4. If the `lastSourceOffset` is null or an empty string, it initializes a new instance of `HashMap<String, String>` and assigns it to the `offsetMap` variable.\n\n5. If the `lastSourceOffset` is not null or an empty string, it uses the `JSON_MAPPER` object (presumably a JSON parsing library) to deserialize the `lastSourceOffset` string into a generic `Map` object using the `readValue` method: `offsetMap = JSON_MAPPER.readValue(lastSourceOffset, Map.class);`.\n\n6. Finally, the method returns the deserialized `offsetMap`.\n\nIn summary, this method takes an input parameter `lastSourceOffset`, which is expected to be a string representation of a map containing offsets. If the input is null or empty, it initializes an empty map; otherwise, it attempts to deserialize the input into a generic map using JSON parsing and returns the resulting map.', 'metric': 0.2401500938086304}